Backport of libuv PR #3250 (commit 9f0101dcb8), the uv__udp_io hunk only.

libuv 1.52.0 (PR #4902, "linux: add MSG_ERRQUEUE ipv4/ipv6 udp support")
changed POLLERR handling: instead of a normal recvmsg (which consumes and
clears the latched socket error via the kernel's sock_error()), POLLERR now
drains ONLY the MSG_ERRQUEUE. On a UDP socket with IP_MTU_DISCOVER=IP_PMTUDISC_PROBE
and no IP_RECVERR -- exactly libudx's data socket (deps/libudx/src/io_posix.c) --
the error queue is empty, so sk_err is never cleared. After an ICMP
frag-needed / socket error on a real (small-MTU / mobile / CGNAT) path the
UDP stream wedges: send() keeps failing, no data flows, no RTO fires, no
close. Same regression class as libuv #5030 (BIND 9, ISC-bisected to the
same commit 80a5e3ba).

Fixed upstream on the v1.x branch by PR #3250. Not in any 1.52.x release as
of 2026-07 (latest tag v1.52.1, crash-guard only). Applies to 1.52.0/1.52.1.
When libuv >=1.52.2 ships the real fix this patch will fail to apply -- that
is the signal to drop the override.
--- a/src/unix/udp.c
+++ b/src/unix/udp.c
@@ -178,6 +178,12 @@
   handle = container_of(w, uv_udp_t, io_watcher);
   assert(handle->type == UV_UDP);
 
+  /* Trigger a recv and send to find out what POLLERR occurred. Restores the
+   * pre-1.52.0 behavior of consuming/clearing the latched socket error via a
+   * normal recv (libuv PR #3250; regression from #4902, see libuv #5030). */
+  if (revents & POLLERR)
+    revents |= POLLIN | POLLOUT;
+
   if (revents & POLLIN)
     uv__udp_recvmsg(handle, 0);
 
